{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"0pNcQ9xH6fl2918Nk6YeDG6iw30=","title":"Move WrenLift onto the core heap","message":"Implement GcAllocator (src/runtime/gc_trait.rs) over caribou::heap; replace\nObjHeader with the descriptor word (ObjClass embeds the descriptor for its\ninstances, so class_of is a pointer subtraction); delete forwarding tables,\nremembered sets, write barriers, shadow-stack scanning, per-GC method-cache\nand inline-cache flushes, and wlift_region escape copies; map ObjFiber onto\ncore fibers.\n\nObjects that keep pointers in Rust containers are invisible to a conservative\ntrace. Flatten the hot types (instance fields, list elements, closure\nupvalues, fiber value stacks) into GC blocks, which also removes the JIT's\ndependency on Vec's private layout (object_layout.rs CLOSURE_UPVALUES_DATA).\nMaps and strings keep their containers behind a Typed trace hook and a\nfinalizer until worth flattening.\n\nGate: WrenLift suite green; delta_blue and allocation-heavy benchmarks within\nan agreed budget, else sticky-mark generational Immix before phase 3.","files":null}]}